---
// Real 404 page. Without a top-level 404.html, Cloudflare Pages served the homepage
// (HTTP 200) for any unknown URL, e.g. /llms.txt before it existed. That reads as a
// "soft 404" to search engines and AI crawlers.
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8"/>
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1.0"/>
  <title>Page Not Found — Sunbright Recovery Center</title>
  <meta name="robots" content="noindex"/>
  <link rel="icon" type="image/png" href="/favicon.png"/>
  <style>
    body{font-family:Inter,system-ui,sans-serif;color:#1a2438;background:#fff;margin:0;display:flex;min-height:100vh;align-items:center;justify-content:center;text-align:center;padding:24px}
    h1{font-family:Lora,Georgia,serif;color:#1a2e5a;font-size:32px;margin:0 0 12px}
    p{color:#3d4a5c;margin:0 0 20px;line-height:1.6}
    a.btn{display:inline-block;background:#1a2e5a;color:#fff;padding:12px 22px;border-radius:999px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600}
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <main>
    <img src="/logo.png" alt="Sunbright Recovery Center" width="160" style="margin-bottom:20px"/>
    <h1>We couldn't find that page.</h1>
    <p>It may have moved. You can head back home, or call us at <a href="tel:+15305134294">(530) 513-4294</a>.</p>
    <a class="btn" href="/">Back to Sunbright</a>
  </main>
</body>
</html>
